          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "guīzé is built from guī and zé, both inherited from Middle Chinese, kjwie and tsok (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'round' and the second 'a rule'."
